    "result_text": "BUILD SUCCESS with all tests green. Done.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec asked to derive an owner's `locality` from `city` via a fixed table (Sydney\u2192NSW, Melbourne\u2192VIC, Brisbane\u2192QLD), returning the canonical region or `UNKNOWN` otherwise. Since locality depends only on the owner's *own* city (like the existing `membershipTier`/`displayName` derived fields, not the persisted `namesakeCount`/`customerCode` which depend on other owners in the DB), the right pattern here is mapper-side derivation \u2014 no entity column, Assign function, or migration needed.\n\nChanges:\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `locality` read-only string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes it.\n2. **`src/main/java/.../model/Locality.java`** (new) \u2014 a small helper holding the fixed `CITY_REGION` table with `Locality.of(city)` returning the region or `\"UNKNOWN\"` (also null-safe).\n3. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 wired the derivation via `@Mapping(target = \"locality\", expression = \"...Locality.of(owner.getCity())\")`, matching the existing expression-based derived fields.\n\nBoth `GET /api/owners/{id}` and the create response flow through `toOwnerDto`, so the value is consistent on read-back. Full test suite: `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 green.",
